  "subject": "svf",
  "summary": "A resonant multimode filter per voice: shapes brightness, usually swept by an envelope.",
  "text": "svf: the filter module kind (svf). A resonant multimode filter per voice: shapes brightness, usually swept by an envelope.\nParameters:\n  mode: lp|bp|hp|notch, default lp. The filter response: lp, bp, hp or notch. [moves spectrum.centroid_hz]\n  cutoff: 20Hz..20kHz, default 2kHz. The corner frequency: lower is darker for a low-pass; route an envelope here for plucks and sweeps. [moves spectrum.centroid_hz]\n  resonance: 0%..100%, default 10%. Emphasis at the cutoff, from none (Q 0.5) to a sharp whistling peak (Q 25).\n  keytrack: 0%..100%, default 0%. How much the cutoff follows the played note: 100 % moves it an octave per octave played.\n  drive: 0dB..24dB, default 0dB. Gain into a soft saturator before the filter, normalised back after: adds grit and harmonics. [moves spectrum.harmonics_db]",
